:Class SSHClient
⍝ SSH-2 client using Dyalog Conga for TCP transport
⍝ Implements the SSH-2 protocol (RFC 4251-4254) over raw TCP

    ⎕ML←⎕IO←1

    ∇ r←Version
    ⍝ Return the current version
      :Access public shared
      r←'SSHClient' '0.1.0' '2026-03-04'
    ∇

⍝ Connection fields
    :field public Host←''                          ⍝ SSH server hostname or IP
    :field public Port←22                          ⍝ SSH server port (default 22)
    :field public Username←''                      ⍝ username for authentication
    :field public Password←''                      ⍝ password for password auth
    :field public KeyFile←''                       ⍝ path to private key file (PEM) for pubkey auth
    :field public KnownHostsFile←''               ⍝ path to known_hosts file for host verification

⍝ Conga-related fields
    :field public BufferSize←200000                ⍝ Conga buffer size
    :field public WaitTime←5000                    ⍝ timeout in ms on Conga Wait calls
    :field public Timeout←30                       ⍝ seconds before overall operation times out
    :field public shared LDRC                      ⍝ reference to Conga LIB instance after init
    :field public shared CongaPath←''             ⍝ path to Conga workspace
    :field public shared CongaRef←''              ⍝ user-supplied reference to Conga
    :field public shared CongaVersion←''          ⍝ Conga [major minor build]

⍝ Operational fields
    :field public shared Debug←0                   ⍝ bitmask: +1=no trapping +2=stop on connect +4=packet +8=crypto

⍝ Internal state
    :field Client←''                               ⍝ Conga client ID
    :field ServerBanner←''                         ⍝ server version string from SSH banner
    :field SessionID←''                            ⍝ session ID (hash from key exchange)
    :field Authenticated←0                         ⍝ 1 if successfully authenticated
    :field ChannelID←¯1                            ⍝ current channel number
    :field RemoteChannelID←¯1                      ⍝ remote channel number from server
    :field RemoteWindowSize←0                      ⍝ remote initial window size

⍝ Crypto state (initialised after NEWKEYS)
    :field CryptoActive←0                            ⍝ 1 after NEWKEYS exchange
    :field SeqSend←0                                 ⍝ client→server packet sequence number
    :field SeqRecv←0                                 ⍝ server→client packet sequence number
    :field AesCtxSend←⍬                              ⍝ AES-128 context for sending
    :field AesCtxRecv←⍬                              ⍝ AES-128 context for receiving
    :field CtrSend←⍬                                 ⍝ AES-CTR counter for sending
    :field CtrRecv←⍬                                 ⍝ AES-CTR counter for receiving
    :field MacKeySend←⍬                              ⍝ HMAC-SHA-256 key for sending
    :field MacKeyRecv←⍬                              ⍝ HMAC-SHA-256 key for receiving

⍝ SFTP state
    :field SFTPActive←0                              ⍝ 1 when SFTP subsystem is active
    :field SFTPChanID←¯1                             ⍝ local channel ID for SFTP
    :field SFTPRemoteChan←¯1                         ⍝ remote channel ID for SFTP
    :field SFTPRemoteWin←0                           ⍝ remote window size for SFTP send
    :field SFTPReqID←0                               ⍝ SFTP request ID counter
    :field SFTPBuf←⍬                                 ⍝ buffered SFTP data from channel
    :field SFTPRecvBuf←⍬                             ⍝ SSH-level receive buffer for SFTP
    :field SFTPReceived←0                            ⍝ bytes received for window management

⍝ SSH-2 message type constants (RFC 4250)
    :field public readonly shared MSG_DISCONNECT←1
    :field public readonly shared MSG_IGNORE←2
    :field public readonly shared MSG_DEBUG←4
    :field public readonly shared MSG_SERVICE_REQUEST←5
    :field public readonly shared MSG_SERVICE_ACCEPT←6
    :field public readonly shared MSG_KEXINIT←20
    :field public readonly shared MSG_NEWKEYS←21
    :field public readonly shared MSG_KEXDH_INIT←30
    :field public readonly shared MSG_KEXDH_REPLY←31
    :field public readonly shared MSG_USERAUTH_REQUEST←50
    :field public readonly shared MSG_USERAUTH_FAILURE←51
    :field public readonly shared MSG_USERAUTH_SUCCESS←52
    :field public readonly shared MSG_CHANNEL_OPEN←90
    :field public readonly shared MSG_CHANNEL_OPEN_CONFIRMATION←91
    :field public readonly shared MSG_CHANNEL_OPEN_FAILURE←92
    :field public readonly shared MSG_CHANNEL_WINDOW_ADJUST←93
    :field public readonly shared MSG_CHANNEL_DATA←94
    :field public readonly shared MSG_CHANNEL_EOF←96
    :field public readonly shared MSG_CHANNEL_CLOSE←97
    :field public readonly shared MSG_CHANNEL_REQUEST←98
    :field public readonly shared MSG_USERAUTH_PK_OK←60
    :field public readonly shared MSG_USERAUTH_BANNER←53
    :field public readonly shared MSG_CHANNEL_SUCCESS←99
    :field public readonly shared MSG_CHANNEL_FAILURE←100
    :field public readonly shared MSG_GLOBAL_REQUEST←80
    :field public readonly shared MSG_REQUEST_FAILURE←82

⍝ SFTP packet types (SSH File Transfer Protocol v3)
    :field public readonly shared FXP_INIT←1
    :field public readonly shared FXP_VERSION←2
    :field public readonly shared FXP_OPEN←3
    :field public readonly shared FXP_CLOSE←4
    :field public readonly shared FXP_READ←5
    :field public readonly shared FXP_WRITE←6
    :field public readonly shared FXP_FSTAT←8
    :field public readonly shared FXP_STATUS←101
    :field public readonly shared FXP_HANDLE←102
    :field public readonly shared FXP_DATA←103
    :field public readonly shared FXP_LSTAT←7
    :field public readonly shared FXP_OPENDIR←11
    :field public readonly shared FXP_READDIR←12
    :field public readonly shared FXP_STAT←17
    :field public readonly shared FXP_ATTRS←105
    :field public readonly shared FXP_NAME←104

⍝ SFTP open flags
    :field public readonly shared FXF_READ←1
    :field public readonly shared FXF_WRITE←2
    :field public readonly shared FXF_CREAT←8
    :field public readonly shared FXF_TRUNC←16

⍝ SFTP status codes
    :field public readonly shared FX_OK←0
    :field public readonly shared FX_EOF←1

    ∇ make
    ⍝ No-argument constructor
      :Access public
      :Implements constructor
    ∇

    ∇ make1 args
    ⍝ Constructor with connection arguments
    ⍝ args - [Host [Port [Username [Password]]]]
      :Access public
      :Implements constructor
      →0⍴⍨0∊⍴args
      args←,⊆args
      :If 2=⌊nameClass⊃args ⍝ array of positional arguments
          (Host Port Username Password)←4↑args,(-4-≢args)↑Host Port Username Password
      :ElseIf 9.1=nameClass⊃args ⍝ namespace of named settings
          args{⍎⍵,'←⍺⍎⍵'}¨(⊃args).⎕NL ¯2.1
      :Else
          'Invalid constructor argument'⎕SIGNAL 11
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ∇ Goodbye
      :Implements destructor
      {}{0::⍬ ⋄ Close⍬}⍣(~0∊⍴Client)⊢''
    ∇

    ∇ {ns}←initResult ns
    ⍝ Initialise the standard result namespace
      :Access shared
      ns.(Host Port Username rc msg Data Elapsed)←'' 22 '' ¯1 '' '' 0
    ∇

    ∇ {r}←setDisplayFormat r;rc;msg;host;data
    ⍝ Set ⎕DF on a result namespace for readable display
      :If 9.1=nameClass r
          rc←'rc: ',⍕r.rc
          msg←' | msg: ',⍕r.msg
          host←' | host: ',(⍕r.Host),':',(⍕r.Port)
          data←' | ',{'≢Data: ',(⍕≢⍵),(9.1=nameClass ⍵)/' (namespace)'}r.Data
          r.⎕DF 1⌽'][',rc,msg,host,data
      :EndIf
    ∇

⍝ ────────────────────────────────────────────────
⍝  Public API
⍝ ────────────────────────────────────────────────

    ∇ r←Connect
    ⍝ Open a TCP connection to the SSH server and complete the SSH handshake + authentication
    ⍝ Returns a result namespace with rc=0 on success
      :Access public
      r←initResult ⎕NS''
      r.(Host Port Username)←Host Port Username
      :Trap (dbg 1)↓0
          →∆END↓⍨0∊⍴(Initialize r).msg  ⍝ ensure Conga is ready
          r←SSHConnect r
      :Else
          r.(rc msg)←¯1('Unexpected ',⊃{⍺,' at ',⍵}/2↑⎕DMX.DM)
      :EndTrap
     ∆END:
      setDisplayFormat r
    ∇

    ∇ r←Exec cmd
    ⍝ Execute a shell command on the remote host over an SSH session-channel
    ⍝ cmd  - character vector command string
    ⍝ Returns result namespace; r.Data contains stdout of the command
      :Access public
      r←initResult ⎕NS''
      :If 0∊⍴Client
          r.(rc msg)←¯1 'Not connected – call Connect first'
          →0
      :EndIf
      :Trap (dbg 1)↓0
          r←cmd SSHExec r
      :Else
          r.(rc msg)←¯1('Unexpected ',⊃{⍺,' at ',⍵}/2↑⎕DMX.DM)
      :EndTrap
      setDisplayFormat r
    ∇

    ∇ r←{opts}GetFile args;remotePath;localPath;handle;offset;data;chunk;sftpMsg;rest;code;id;dummy;tn;msgText;done
    ⍝ SFTP download – transfer a file from the remote host
    ⍝ args    - (RemotePath LocalPath) or just RemotePath (saves to current directory)
    ⍝ opts    - optional namespace of options
      :Access public
      :If 0=⎕NC'opts' ⋄ opts←⎕NS'' ⋄ :EndIf
      r←initResult ⎕NS''
      :If 0∊⍴Client
          r.(rc msg)←¯1 'Not connected – call Connect first' ⋄ →0
      :EndIf
      :Trap (dbg 1)↓0
          args←,⊆args
          remotePath←⊃args
          :If 1<≢args ⋄ localPath←2⊃args
          :Else ⋄ localPath←⊃⌽'/'(≠⊆⊢)remotePath
          :EndIf

          ⍝ Open SFTP session
          →0↓⍨0∊⍴(SFTPOpenSession r).msg

          ⍝ Open remote file for reading
          id←NextSFTPID
          {}SFTPSend∊((,FXP_OPEN),(EncodeUint32 id)
                     (EncodeString remotePath)
                     (EncodeUint32 FXF_READ)
                     (EncodeUint32 0))
          sftpMsg←SFTPRecv
          :If FXP_STATUS=⊃sftpMsg
              rest←1↓sftpMsg
              (dummy rest)←DecodeUint32 rest
              (code rest)←DecodeUint32 rest
              (msgText rest)←DecodeString rest
              r.(rc msg)←¯1('SFTP open failed: ',msgText)
              SFTPCloseSession ⋄ →0
          :ElseIf FXP_HANDLE≠⊃sftpMsg
              r.(rc msg)←¯1('Expected FXP_HANDLE, got type ',⍕⊃sftpMsg)
              SFTPCloseSession ⋄ →0
          :EndIf
          rest←1↓sftpMsg
          (dummy rest)←DecodeUint32 rest
          (handle rest)←DecodeStringRaw rest

          ⍝ Read file data in chunks
          offset←0 ⋄ data←⍬ ⋄ done←0
          :While ~done
              id←NextSFTPID
              {}SFTPSend∊((,FXP_READ),(EncodeUint32 id)
                         (EncodeStringBytes handle)
                         (EncodeUint64 offset)
                         (EncodeUint32 30000))
              sftpMsg←SFTPRecv
              :If FXP_DATA=⊃sftpMsg
                  rest←1↓sftpMsg
                  (dummy rest)←DecodeUint32 rest
                  (chunk rest)←DecodeStringRaw rest
                  data,←chunk
                  offset+←≢chunk
              :ElseIf FXP_STATUS=⊃sftpMsg
                  rest←1↓sftpMsg
                  (dummy rest)←DecodeUint32 rest
                  (code rest)←DecodeUint32 rest
                  :If FX_EOF=code
                      done←1
                  :Else
                      (msgText rest)←DecodeString rest
                      r.(rc msg)←¯1('SFTP read error: ',msgText)
                      {}SFTPSend∊(,FXP_CLOSE),(EncodeUint32 NextSFTPID),(EncodeStringBytes handle)
                      {}SFTPRecv
                      SFTPCloseSession ⋄ →0
                  :EndIf
              :EndIf
          :EndWhile

          ⍝ Close remote file handle
          {}SFTPSend∊(,FXP_CLOSE),(EncodeUint32 NextSFTPID),(EncodeStringBytes handle)
          {}SFTPRecv

          ⍝ Close SFTP session
          SFTPCloseSession

          ⍝ Write to local file
          :If ⎕NEXISTS localPath ⋄ tn←localPath ⎕NTIE 0 ⋄ 0 ⎕NRESIZE tn
          :Else ⋄ tn←localPath ⎕NCREATE 0
          :EndIf
          (⎕UCS data) ⎕NAPPEND tn 80
          ⎕NUNTIE tn

          r.(rc msg Data)←0 '' localPath
      :Else
          r.(rc msg)←¯1('Unexpected ',⊃{⍺,' at ',⍵}/2↑⎕DMX.DM)
      :EndTrap
      setDisplayFormat r
    ∇

    ∇ r←{opts}PutFile args;localPath;remotePath;handle;offset;data;chunk;sftpMsg;rest;code;id;dummy;tn;msgText;chunkSize
    ⍝ SFTP upload – transfer a file to the remote host
    ⍝ args    - (LocalPath RemotePath) or just LocalPath (uses basename on remote)
    ⍝ opts    - optional namespace of options
      :Access public
      :If 0=⎕NC'opts' ⋄ opts←⎕NS'' ⋄ :EndIf
      r←initResult ⎕NS''
      :If 0∊⍴Client
          r.(rc msg)←¯1 'Not connected – call Connect first' ⋄ →0
      :EndIf
      :Trap (dbg 1)↓0
          args←,⊆args
          localPath←⊃args
          :If 1<≢args ⋄ remotePath←2⊃args
          :Else ⋄ remotePath←⊃⌽'/'(≠⊆⊢)localPath
          :EndIf

          ⍝ Read local file
          :If ~⎕NEXISTS localPath
              r.(rc msg)←¯1('Local file not found: ',localPath) ⋄ →0
          :EndIf
          tn←localPath ⎕NTIE 0
          data←⎕UCS ⎕NREAD tn 80(⎕NSIZE tn)0
          ⎕NUNTIE tn
          :If dbg 4
              ⎕←'DBG PutFile: data DR=',(⍕⎕DR data),' shape=',(⍕⍴data),' depth=',⍕≡data
              ⎕←'DBG PutFile: first 20 values=',⍕20↑data
              ⎕←'DBG PutFile: type of ⊃data = ',⍕⎕DR⊃data
          :EndIf

          ⍝ Open SFTP session
          →0↓⍨0∊⍴(SFTPOpenSession r).msg

          ⍝ Open remote file for writing (create + truncate)
          id←NextSFTPID
          {}SFTPSend∊((,FXP_OPEN),(EncodeUint32 id)
                     (EncodeString remotePath)
                     (EncodeUint32 FXF_WRITE+FXF_CREAT+FXF_TRUNC)
                     (EncodeUint32 0))
          sftpMsg←SFTPRecv
          :If FXP_STATUS=⊃sftpMsg
              rest←1↓sftpMsg
              (dummy rest)←DecodeUint32 rest
              (code rest)←DecodeUint32 rest
              (msgText rest)←DecodeString rest
              r.(rc msg)←¯1('SFTP open for write failed: ',msgText)
              SFTPCloseSession ⋄ →0
          :ElseIf FXP_HANDLE≠⊃sftpMsg
              r.(rc msg)←¯1('Expected FXP_HANDLE, got type ',⍕⊃sftpMsg)
              SFTPCloseSession ⋄ →0
          :EndIf
          rest←1↓sftpMsg
          (dummy rest)←DecodeUint32 rest
          (handle rest)←DecodeStringRaw rest

          ⍝ Write data in chunks
          offset←0 ⋄ chunkSize←30000
          :While offset<≢data
              chunk←chunkSize⌊(≢data)-offset
              id←NextSFTPID
              {}SFTPSend∊((,FXP_WRITE),(EncodeUint32 id)
                         (EncodeStringBytes handle)
                         (EncodeUint64 offset)
                         (EncodeStringBytes chunk↑offset↓data))
              sftpMsg←SFTPRecv
              :If FXP_STATUS≠⊃sftpMsg
                  r.(rc msg)←¯1('Expected FXP_STATUS for write, got type ',⍕⊃sftpMsg)
                  {}SFTPSend∊(,FXP_CLOSE),(EncodeUint32 NextSFTPID),(EncodeStringBytes handle)
                  {}SFTPRecv
                  SFTPCloseSession ⋄ →0
              :EndIf
              rest←1↓sftpMsg
              (dummy rest)←DecodeUint32 rest
              (code rest)←DecodeUint32 rest
              :If FX_OK≠code
                  (msgText rest)←DecodeString rest
                  r.(rc msg)←¯1('SFTP write error: ',msgText)
                  {}SFTPSend∊(,FXP_CLOSE),(EncodeUint32 NextSFTPID),(EncodeStringBytes handle)
                  {}SFTPRecv
                  SFTPCloseSession ⋄ →0
              :EndIf
              offset+←chunk
          :EndWhile

          ⍝ Close remote file handle
          {}SFTPSend∊(,FXP_CLOSE),(EncodeUint32 NextSFTPID),(EncodeStringBytes handle)
          {}SFTPRecv

          ⍝ Close SFTP session
          SFTPCloseSession

          r.(rc msg Data)←0 '' remotePath
      :Else
          r.(rc msg)←¯1('Unexpected ',⊃{⍺,' at ',⍵}/2↑⎕DMX.DM)
      :EndTrap
      setDisplayFormat r
    ∇

    ∇ r←ListDir path;handle;sftpMsg;rest;code;id;dummy;msgText;entries;count;i;fname;lname;attrs;entry
    ⍝ SFTP directory listing
    ⍝ path    - remote directory path
    ⍝ Returns result namespace; r.Data is a vector of namespaces (name longname size permissions mtime …)
      :Access public
      r←initResult ⎕NS''
      :If 0∊⍴Client
          r.(rc msg)←¯1 'Not connected – call Connect first' ⋄ →0
      :EndIf
      :Trap (dbg 1)↓0
          ⍝ Open SFTP session
          →0↓⍨0∊⍴(SFTPOpenSession r).msg

          ⍝ Open directory
          id←NextSFTPID
          {}SFTPSend∊((,FXP_OPENDIR),(EncodeUint32 id),(EncodeString path))
          sftpMsg←SFTPRecv
          :If FXP_STATUS=⊃sftpMsg
              rest←1↓sftpMsg
              (dummy rest)←DecodeUint32 rest
              (code rest)←DecodeUint32 rest
              (msgText rest)←DecodeString rest
              r.(rc msg)←¯1('SFTP opendir failed: ',msgText)
              SFTPCloseSession ⋄ →0
          :ElseIf FXP_HANDLE≠⊃sftpMsg
              r.(rc msg)←¯1('Expected FXP_HANDLE, got type ',⍕⊃sftpMsg)
              SFTPCloseSession ⋄ →0
          :EndIf
          rest←1↓sftpMsg
          (dummy rest)←DecodeUint32 rest
          (handle rest)←DecodeStringRaw rest

          ⍝ Read directory entries
          entries←⍬
          :While 1
              id←NextSFTPID
              {}SFTPSend∊((,FXP_READDIR),(EncodeUint32 id),(EncodeStringBytes handle))
              sftpMsg←SFTPRecv
              :If FXP_NAME=⊃sftpMsg
                  rest←1↓sftpMsg
                  (dummy rest)←DecodeUint32 rest   ⍝ request id
                  (count rest)←DecodeUint32 rest
                  :For i :In ⍳count
                      (fname rest)←DecodeString rest
                      (lname rest)←DecodeString rest
                      (attrs rest)←DecodeAttrs rest
                      entry←⎕NS''
                      entry.name←fname
                      entry.longname←lname
                      entry.(size uid gid permissions atime mtime)←attrs.(size uid gid permissions atime mtime)
                      entries,←entry
                  :EndFor
              :ElseIf FXP_STATUS=⊃sftpMsg
                  rest←1↓sftpMsg
                  (dummy rest)←DecodeUint32 rest
                  (code rest)←DecodeUint32 rest
                  :If FX_EOF=code
                      :Leave
                  :Else
                      (msgText rest)←DecodeString rest
                      r.(rc msg)←¯1('SFTP readdir error: ',msgText)
                      {}SFTPSend∊(,FXP_CLOSE),(EncodeUint32 NextSFTPID),(EncodeStringBytes handle)
                      {}SFTPRecv
                      SFTPCloseSession ⋄ →0
                  :EndIf
              :EndIf
          :EndWhile

          ⍝ Close directory handle
          {}SFTPSend∊(,FXP_CLOSE),(EncodeUint32 NextSFTPID),(EncodeStringBytes handle)
          {}SFTPRecv

          ⍝ Close SFTP session
          SFTPCloseSession

          r.(rc msg Data)←0 '' entries
      :Else
          r.(rc msg)←¯1('Unexpected ',⊃{⍺,' at ',⍵}/2↑⎕DMX.DM)
      :EndTrap
      setDisplayFormat r
    ∇

    ∇ r←Stat path;sftpMsg;rest;code;id;dummy;msgText;attrs
    ⍝ SFTP stat – get file/directory attributes
    ⍝ path    - remote file or directory path
    ⍝ Returns result namespace; r.Data is a namespace with size uid gid permissions atime mtime
      :Access public
      r←initResult ⎕NS''
      :If 0∊⍴Client
          r.(rc msg)←¯1 'Not connected – call Connect first' ⋄ →0
      :EndIf
      :Trap (dbg 1)↓0
          ⍝ Open SFTP session
          →0↓⍨0∊⍴(SFTPOpenSession r).msg

          ⍝ Send FXP_STAT
          id←NextSFTPID
          {}SFTPSend∊((,FXP_STAT),(EncodeUint32 id),(EncodeString path))
          sftpMsg←SFTPRecv
          :If FXP_ATTRS=⊃sftpMsg
              rest←1↓sftpMsg
              (dummy rest)←DecodeUint32 rest   ⍝ request id
              (attrs rest)←DecodeAttrs rest
              r.(rc msg Data)←0 '' attrs
          :ElseIf FXP_STATUS=⊃sftpMsg
              rest←1↓sftpMsg
              (dummy rest)←DecodeUint32 rest
              (code rest)←DecodeUint32 rest
              (msgText rest)←DecodeString rest
              r.(rc msg)←¯1('SFTP stat failed: ',msgText)
          :Else
              r.(rc msg)←¯1('Expected FXP_ATTRS, got type ',⍕⊃sftpMsg)
          :EndIf

          ⍝ Close SFTP session
          SFTPCloseSession
      :Else
          r.(rc msg)←¯1('Unexpected ',⊃{⍺,' at ',⍵}/2↑⎕DMX.DM)
      :EndTrap
      setDisplayFormat r
    ∇

    ∇ r←Close
    ⍝ Send SSH_MSG_DISCONNECT then close the Conga client
    ⍝ Returns result namespace with rc=0 on success
      :Access public
      r←initResult ⎕NS''
      r.(Host Port Username)←Host Port Username
      :If 0∊⍴Client
          r.(rc msg)←0 'Already disconnected'
          setDisplayFormat r ⋄ →0
      :EndIf
      :If SFTPActive ⋄ SFTPCloseSession ⋄ :EndIf
      r.msg←'Disconnected'
      :Trap 0
          {}SendPacket SSHDisconnectPacket 11 'Connection closed by client' ⍝ 11 = BY_APPLICATION
      :Else
          r.msg←'Disconnected (disconnect packet failed: ',⎕DMX.EM,')'
      :EndTrap
      :Trap 0
          {}LDRC.Close Client
      :Else
          r.msg,←' (close failed: ',⎕DMX.EM,')'
      :EndTrap
      Client←''
      Authenticated←0
      ChannelID←¯1
      RemoteChannelID←¯1
      r.rc←0
      setDisplayFormat r
    ∇

    ∇ r←Config
    ⍝ Return current configuration as a matrix of name/value pairs
      :Access public
      r←↑{6::⍵'not set' ⋄ ⍵(⍎⍵)}¨⎕THIS.⎕NL ¯2.2
    ∇

⍝ ────────────────────────────────────────────────
⍝  Shared convenience methods (call without instance)
⍝ ────────────────────────────────────────────────

    ∇ r←New args
    ⍝ Create a new SSHClient instance
    ⍝ args - same as constructor args
      :Access public shared
      r←''
      :Trap (dbg 1)↓0
          r←##.⎕NEW(⊃⊃⎕CLASS ⎕THIS)(,⊆args)
      :Else
          r←initResult ⎕NS''
          r.(rc msg)←¯1 ⎕DMX.EM
      :EndTrap
    ∇

    ∇ r←Do args
    ⍝ Create instance, connect, run a command, and close – all in one call
    ⍝ args - (Host Command) | (Host Username Password Command) | namespace
      :Access public shared
      r←initResult ⎕NS''
      :Trap (dbg 1)↓0
          :If 9.1=nameClass⊃,⊆args
              r←New⊃,⊆args
          :Else
              args←,⊆args
              r←New(2↑args)   ⍝ Host and (optional) Port
              :If 9.1≠nameClass r
                  r.Username Password←2↑2↓args  ⍝ Username Password
              :EndIf
          :EndIf
          →0⍴⍨9.1≠nameClass r ⍝ bail if New returned an error namespace
          :If 0≠(r.Connect).rc ⋄ →0 ⋄ :EndIf
          r←r.Exec⊃¯1↑,⊆args ⍝ last element is the command
          r.Close
      :Else
          r.(rc msg)←¯1 ⎕DMX.EM
      :EndTrap
    ∇

⍝ ────────────────────────────────────────────────
⍝  Conga initialisation  (adapted from HttpCommand)
⍝ ────────────────────────────────────────────────

    ∇ r←Init
    ⍝ Explicitly initialise Conga; returns (rc msg)
      :Access public
      r←(Initialize initResult ⎕NS'').(rc msg)
      r[1]×←~0∊⍴2⊃r
    ∇

    ∇ r←Initialize r;ref;root;nc;n;ns;copied;class;path
    ⍝ Ensure LDRC is a live Conga reference
      r.msg←''
      :Hold 'SSHClientInit'
          :If {6 16 999::1 ⋄ ''≡LDRC:1 ⋄ 0⊣LDRC.Describe'.'}''
              LDRC←''
              :If ~0∊⍴CongaRef
                  :If 0∊⍴LDRC←r ResolveCongaRef CongaRef
                      r.msg,⍨←'Could not initialise Conga using CongaRef "',(⍕CongaRef),'" due to '
                      →∆END
                  :EndIf
              :Else
                  :For root :In ## #
                      ref nc←root{1↑¨⍵{(×⍵)∘/¨⍺ ⍵}⍺.⎕NC ⍵}ns←'Conga' 'DRC'
                      :If 9=⊃⌊nc ⋄ :Leave ⋄ :EndIf
                  :EndFor
                  :If 9=⊃⌊nc
                      :If 0∊⍴LDRC←r ResolveCongaRef(root⍎∊ref)
                          →∆END⊣r.msg,⍨←'Could not initialise Conga from "',(∊(⍕root)'.'ref),'" due to '
                      :EndIf
                      →∆COPY↓⍨{999::0 ⋄ 1⊣LDRC.Describe'.'}''
                  :Else
     ∆COPY:
                      class←⊃⊃⎕CLASS ⎕THIS
                      :If ~0∊⍴CongaPath
                          CongaPath←∊1 ⎕NPARTS CongaPath,'/'
                          →∆END↓⍨0∊⍴r.msg←(~⎕NEXISTS CongaPath)/'CongaPath "',CongaPath,'" does not exist'
                      :EndIf
                      copied←0
                      :For n :In ns
                          :For path :In (1+0∊⍴CongaPath)⊃(⊂CongaPath)((dyalogRoot,'ws/')'')
                              :Trap (dbg 1)↓0
                                  n class.⎕CY path,'conga'
                                  LDRC←r ResolveCongaRef(class⍎n)
                                  :If 0∊⍴LDRC
                                      r.msg,⍨←n,' was copied from "',path,'conga", but encountered '
                                      →∆END
                                  :EndIf
                                  →∆COPIED⊣copied←1
                              :EndTrap
                          :EndFor
                      :EndFor
                      →∆END↓⍨0∊⍴r.msg←(~copied)/'neither Conga nor DRC were successfully copied'
     ∆COPIED:
                  :EndIf
              :EndIf
          :EndIf
          CongaVersion←LDRC.Version
          :If 0≠⊃LDRC.SetProp'.' 'EventMode' 1
              r.msg←'Unable to set EventMode on Conga root'
          :EndIf
     ∆END:
      :EndHold
    ∇

    ∇ LDRC←r ResolveCongaRef CongaRef;failed;z
    ⍝ Resolve CongaRef to a live Conga LIB reference
      LDRC←'' ⋄ failed←0
      :Select nameClass CongaRef
      :Case 9.1 ⍝ namespace (DRC or Conga)
     ∆TRY:
          :Trap (dbg 1)↓0
              :If 2 3≢⌊CongaRef.⎕NC'DllVer' 'Init'
                  r.msg←'does not refer to a valid Conga interface'
                  →∆EXIT⊣LDRC←''
              :EndIf
              :If ∨/'.Conga'⍷⍕CongaRef
                  LDRC←CongaPath CongaRef.Init'SSHClient'
              :ElseIf 0≡⊃CongaRef.Init CongaPath
                  LDRC←CongaRef
              :Else
                  r.msg←'does not refer to a valid Conga interface'
                  →∆EXIT⊣LDRC←''
              :End
          :Else
              :If failed
                  →∆EXIT⊣LDRC←''⊣r.msg←∊{⍺,(~0∊⍴⍵)/': ',⍵}/⎕DMX.(EM Message)
              :Else
                  →∆TRY⊣failed←1
              :EndIf
          :EndTrap
      :Case 9.2 ⍝ already an initialised instance
          :If 3=⌊|CongaRef.⎕NC⊂'Clt'
              LDRC←CongaRef
          :EndIf
      :Case 2.1 ⍝ character name
          :Trap (dbg 1)↓0
              :If 9≠z←⎕NC⍕CongaRef
                  →∆EXIT⊣r.msg←'CongaRef ',(1+z=0)⊃'is invalid' 'was not found'
              :EndIf
              LDRC←r ResolveCongaRef(⍎∊⍕CongaRef)
          :Else
              r.msg←∊{⍺,(~0∊⍴⍵)/': ',⍵}/⎕DMX.(EM Message)
          :EndTrap
      :EndSelect
     ∆EXIT:
    ∇

⍝ ────────────────────────────────────────────────
⍝  Internal SSH protocol methods
⍝ ────────────────────────────────────────────────

    ∇ r←SSHConnect r;err;rc;starttime;donetime
    ⍝ Open TCP connection then drive the SSH-2 handshake and authentication
      starttime←⎕AI[3]
      donetime←⌊starttime+1000×|Timeout

      ⍝ ── Step 1: open raw TCP connection ──────────────────────────────
      :If 0∊⍴Client
          stopIf dbg 2
          :If 0≠⊃(err Client)←2↑LDRC.Clt''(⍕Host)Port'raw'BufferSize
              Client←''
              →∆END⊣r.(rc msg)←err('TCP connect to ',(⍕Host),':',(⍕Port),' failed')
          :EndIf
      :EndIf

      ⍝ ── Step 2: SSH banner exchange ─────────────────────────────────
      ⍝ RFC 4253 §4.2  – send our identification string, read server's
      →∆END↓⍨0∊⍴r.msg←(SSHBannerExchange r).msg

      ⍝ ── Step 3: key exchange (KEX) ───────────────────────────────────
      ⍝ RFC 4253 §6-9  – negotiate algorithms, perform DH key exchange
      →∆END↓⍨0∊⍴r.msg←(SSHKeyExchange r).msg

      ⍝ ── Step 4: request 'ssh-userauth' service ───────────────────────
      ⍝ RFC 4252 §5
      →∆END↓⍨0∊⍴r.msg←(SSHServiceRequest 'ssh-userauth').msg

      ⍝ ── Step 5: user authentication ──────────────────────────────────
      →∆END↓⍨0∊⍴r.msg←(SSHAuthenticate r).msg

      r.Elapsed←⎕AI[3]-starttime
      r.rc←0
     ∆END:
    ∇

    ∇ r←SSHBannerExchange r;rc;obj;evt;data;buf;lines;banner
    ⍝ RFC 4253 §4.2  Exchange identification strings
    ⍝ Client sends:  SSH-2.0-DyalogSSHClient_0.1\r\n
    ⍝ Server sends:  SSH-2.0-<server-version>\r\n
      ⍝ 1. Send client identification string
      :If 0≠⊃LDRC.Send Client('SSH-2.0-DyalogSSHClient_0.1',⎕UCS 13 10)
          r.(rc msg)←¯1 'Failed to send SSH client banner'
          →0
      :EndIf
      ⍝ 2. Accumulate received data until the server banner line arrives
      ⍝    Server MAY send informational lines before 'SSH-2.0-' (RFC 4253 §4.2)
      buf←''
      :Repeat
          (rc obj evt data)←4↑LDRC.Wait Client
          :If 0≠rc
              r.(rc msg)←rc 'Timeout or error waiting for SSH server banner'
              →0
          :EndIf
          :If evt≡'Block' ⋄ buf,←⎕UCS data ⋄ :EndIf
      :Until ∨/'SSH-2.0-'⍷buf
      ⍝ 3. Extract the banner line (first line starting with 'SSH-2.0-')
      lines←(⎕UCS 10)(≠⊆⊢)buf
      banner←⊃({⊃'SSH-2.0-'⍷⍵}¨lines)/lines
      ⍝ 4. Strip trailing CR and save
      ServerBanner←banner~(⎕UCS 13)
      r.msg←''
    ∇

    ∇ r←SSHKeyExchange r;p;g;x;e;f;K;KS;sigH;V_C;V_S;I_C;I_S;H;⎕FR;k;⎕RL;⎕DCT;b
                       ;cookie;kexPayload;payload;rest;buf;fh;ekc;eks
                       ;ksBytes;ksRest;keyAlgo;keyE;keyN;sigBytes;sigRest;sigAlgo;sigRaw
    ⍝ RFC 4253 §§6-9  Algorithm negotiation and Diffie-Hellman key exchange
    ⍝ Performs diffie-hellman-group14-sha256; derives session keys via SHA-256
    ⍝ Verifies host key signature via RSA PKCS#1 v1.5 SHA-256
    
      ⍝ ── DH group14 prime p (RFC 3526 §3, 2048-bit) ───────────────────
      ⎕FR←1287 ⋄ ⎕DCT←0
      k←(
      'FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFC90FDAA22168C234C4C6628B80DC1CD1'
      '29024E088A67CC74020BBEA63B139B22514A08798E3404DD'
      'EF9519B3CD3A431B302B0A6DF25F14374FE1356D6D51C245'
      'E485B576625E7EC6F44C42E9A637ED6B0BFF5CB6F406B7ED'
      'EE386BFB5A899FA5AE9F24117C4B1FE649286651ECE45B3D'
      'C2007CB8A163BF0598DA48361C55D39A69163FA8FD24CF5F'
      '83655D23DCA3AD961C62F356208552BB9ED529077096966D'
      '670C354E4ABC9804F1746C08CA18217C32905E462E36CE3B'
      'E39E772C180E86039B2783A2EC07A28FB5C55DF06F4C52C9'
      'DE2BCBF6955817183995497CEA956AE515D2261898FA0510'
      '15728E5A8AACAA68FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF'
    )
      p←16⊥¨{(2/(⍳0.5×≢⍵))⊆⍵}(¯1+(⎕D,⎕A)⍳⊢)∊k
      g←2

      ⍝ ── Step 1: build and send SSH_MSG_KEXINIT (RFC 4253 §7.1) ───────
      ⍝fh←⎕NTIE'/dev/urandom' ⋄ cookie←⎕NREAD fh 83 16 0 ⋄ ⎕NUNTIE fh
      ⎕RL←⍬ 2
      cookie←⎕IO-⍨?16⍴256
      kexPayload←∊((,MSG_KEXINIT),cookie
                 (EncodeString 'diffie-hellman-group14-sha256')
                 (EncodeString 'rsa-sha2-256')
                 (EncodeString 'aes128-ctr'),(EncodeString 'aes128-ctr')
                 (EncodeString 'hmac-sha2-256'),(EncodeString 'hmac-sha2-256')
                 (EncodeString 'none'),(EncodeString 'none')
                 (EncodeString ''),(EncodeString '')
                 (EncodeBoolean 0),(EncodeUint32 0))
      I_C←kexPayload
      :If 0≠SendPacket kexPayload
          r.(rc msg)←¯1 'Failed to send KEXINIT' ⋄ →0
      :EndIf

      ⍝ ── Step 2: receive server SSH_MSG_KEXINIT ───────────────────────
      buf←⍬
      (payload buf)←RecvPacket buf
      :If MSG_KEXINIT≠⊃payload
          r.(rc msg)←¯1('Expected KEXINIT(20), got type ',⍕⊃payload) ⋄ →0
      :EndIf
      I_S←payload   ⍝ full payload saved for exchange hash
      
      ⍝ ── Step 3a-b: DH private key x, public value e = g^x mod p ──────
      ⍝fh←⎕NTIE'/dev/urandom' ⋄ x←256⊥⎕NREAD fh 83 32 0 ⋄ ⎕NUNTIE fh
      ⍝÷0
      b←⎕IO-⍨?32⍴256
      e←PowMod((ToBEBytes g) b p)
      ⍝÷0
      :If 0≠SendPacket(,MSG_KEXDH_INIT),EncodeMpInt e
          r.(rc msg)←¯1 'Failed to send KEXDH_INIT' ⋄ →0
      :EndIf

      ⍝ ── Step 3c: receive SSH_MSG_KEXDH_REPLY ─────────────────────────
      (payload buf)←RecvPacket buf
      :If MSG_KEXDH_REPLY≠⊃payload
          r.(rc msg)←¯1('Expected KEXDH_REPLY(31), got type ',⍕⊃payload) ⋄ →0
      :EndIf
      ⍝÷0
      rest←1↓payload
      (KS rest)←DecodeString rest   ⍝ server host-key blob (K_S)
      (f rest)←DecodeMpIntBytes rest ⍝ server DH public value (raw bytes)
      (sigH rest)←DecodeString rest ⍝ signature of exchange hash


      ⍝ ── Step 3d: shared secret K = f^x mod p ─────────────────────────
      K←PowMod(f b p)

      ⍝ ── Step 3e: sigH verification is deferred until after H is computed

      ⍝ ── Step 3f: exchange hash H = SHA-256(V_C||V_S||I_C||I_S||K_S||e||f||K)
      V_C←'SSH-2.0-DyalogSSHClient_0.1'
      V_S←ServerBanner
      H←sha256∊((EncodeString V_C),(EncodeString V_S)
               (EncodeString ⎕UCS I_C),(EncodeString ⎕UCS I_S)
               (EncodeString KS)
               (EncodeMpInt e),(EncodeMpInt f),(EncodeMpInt K))
      :If 0∊⍴SessionID ⋄ SessionID←H ⋄ :EndIf   ⍝ session ID = first H

      ⍝ ── Step 3g: verify host key signature sigH against H ────────────
      ksBytes←⎕UCS KS
      (keyAlgo ksRest)←DecodeString ksBytes
      (keyE ksRest)←DecodeStringRaw ksRest
      (keyN ksRest)←DecodeStringRaw ksRest
      sigBytes←⎕UCS sigH
      (sigAlgo sigRest)←DecodeString sigBytes
      (sigRaw sigRest)←DecodeStringRaw sigRest
      :If ~RsaSha256Verify keyN keyE sigRaw H
          r.(rc msg)←¯1 'Host key signature verification failed' ⋄ →0
      :EndIf

      ⍝ ── Step 4: exchange SSH_MSG_NEWKEYS ─────────────────────────────
      :If 0≠SendPacket,MSG_NEWKEYS
          r.(rc msg)←¯1 'Failed to send NEWKEYS' ⋄ →0
      :EndIf
      (payload buf)←RecvPacket buf
      :If MSG_NEWKEYS≠⊃payload
          r.(rc msg)←¯1('Expected NEWKEYS(21), got type ',⍕⊃payload) ⋄ →0
      :EndIf

      ⍝ ── Step 5: derive session keys and activate encryption ─────────
      ⍝ Key = SHA-256(mpint(K) || H || letter || session_id)
      CtrSend←16↑sha256(EncodeMpInt K),H,65,SessionID     ⍝ IV  C→S  (A)
      CtrRecv←16↑sha256(EncodeMpInt K),H,66,SessionID     ⍝ IV  S→C  (B)
      ekc←16↑sha256(EncodeMpInt K),H,67,SessionID         ⍝ Enc C→S  (C)
      eks←16↑sha256(EncodeMpInt K),H,68,SessionID         ⍝ Enc S→C  (D)
      MacKeySend←sha256(EncodeMpInt K),H,69,SessionID     ⍝ MAC C→S  (E)
      MacKeyRecv←sha256(EncodeMpInt K),H,70,SessionID     ⍝ MAC S→C  (F)
      InitCrypto ekc eks
      CryptoActive←1
      r.msg←''
    ∇

    ∇ r←SSHServiceRequest service;payload;buf
    ⍝ RFC 4253 §10  Request a named SSH service (e.g. 'ssh-userauth')
      r←⎕NS''
      :If 0≠SendPacket(,MSG_SERVICE_REQUEST),EncodeString service
          r.msg←'Failed to send SERVICE_REQUEST' ⋄ →0
      :EndIf
      buf←⍬
      (payload buf)←RecvPacket buf
      :If MSG_DISCONNECT=⊃payload
          r.msg←'Server disconnected during SERVICE_REQUEST' ⋄ →0
      :EndIf
      :If MSG_SERVICE_ACCEPT≠⊃payload
          r.msg←'Expected SERVICE_ACCEPT(6), got type ',⍕⊃payload ⋄ →0
      :EndIf
      r.msg←''
    ∇

    ∇ r←SSHAuthenticate r;home
    ⍝ RFC 4252  User authentication
    ⍝ Tries public-key auth if KeyFile is set; falls back to password auth
    ⍝ Auto-discovers ~/.ssh/id_rsa if no credentials specified
      :If ~0∊⍴Password
          r←SSHAuthPassword r
      :ElseIf ~0∊⍴KeyFile
          r←SSHAuthPublicKey r
      :Else
          home←GetEnv'HOME'
          :If (~0∊⍴home)∧⎕NEXISTS home,'/.ssh/id_rsa'
              KeyFile←home,'/.ssh/id_rsa'
              r←SSHAuthPublicKey r
          :Else
              r.msg←'No credentials supplied'
          :EndIf
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ∇ r←SSHAuthPassword r;payload;buf
    ⍝ RFC 4252 §8  Password authentication method
      payload←∊((,MSG_USERAUTH_REQUEST)
               (EncodeString Username)
               (EncodeString'ssh-connection')
               (EncodeString'password')
               (EncodeBoolean 0)
               (EncodeString Password))
      :If 0≠SendPacket payload
          r.msg←'Failed to send USERAUTH_REQUEST' ⋄ →0
      :EndIf
      buf←⍬
      (payload buf)←RecvPacket buf
      :If MSG_USERAUTH_SUCCESS=⊃payload
          Authenticated←1
          r.msg←''
      :ElseIf MSG_USERAUTH_FAILURE=⊃payload
          r.msg←'Authentication failed'
      :ElseIf MSG_DISCONNECT=⊃payload
          r.msg←'Server disconnected during authentication'
      :Else
          r.msg←'Unexpected message type ',⍕⊃payload
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ∇ r←SSHAuthPublicKey r;key;pubKeyBlob;probePayload;payload;buf;dataToSign;sigBytes;sigBlob;authPayload
    ⍝ RFC 4252 §7  Public-key authentication method
    ⍝ Uses PKCS#1 v1.5 RSA signing with SHA-256 via existing PowMod + sha256
      :Trap (dbg 1)↓0
          key←ParseOpenSSHKey KeyFile
      :Else
          r.msg←'Failed to parse key file: ',⊃⎕DMX.DM ⋄ →0
      :EndTrap

      ⍝ Build public key blob: "ssh-rsa" || e || n
      pubKeyBlob←∊(EncodeString'ssh-rsa')(EncodeMpInt key.e)(EncodeMpInt key.n)

      ⍝ Step 1: Send probe (no signature) to check if server accepts this key
      probePayload←∊((,MSG_USERAUTH_REQUEST)
                    (EncodeString Username)
                    (EncodeString'ssh-connection')
                    (EncodeString'publickey')
                    (EncodeBoolean 0)
                    (EncodeString'rsa-sha2-256')
                    (EncodeStringBytes pubKeyBlob))
      :If 0≠SendPacket probePayload
          r.msg←'Failed to send publickey probe' ⋄ →0
      :EndIf

      ⍝ Step 2: Expect MSG_USERAUTH_PK_OK (60)
      buf←⍬
      (payload buf)←RecvPacket buf
      :While MSG_USERAUTH_BANNER=⊃payload  ⍝ skip server banners (53)
          (payload buf)←RecvPacket buf
      :EndWhile
      :If MSG_USERAUTH_PK_OK≠⊃payload
          :If MSG_USERAUTH_FAILURE=⊃payload
              r.msg←'Server rejected public key'
          :ElseIf MSG_DISCONNECT=⊃payload
              r.msg←'Server disconnected during publickey probe'
          :Else
              r.msg←'Expected USERAUTH_PK_OK(60), got type ',⍕⊃payload
          :EndIf
          →0
      :EndIf

      ⍝ Step 3: Build data to sign (RFC 4252 §7)
      dataToSign←∊((EncodeStringBytes SessionID)
                   (,MSG_USERAUTH_REQUEST)
                   (EncodeString Username)
                   (EncodeString'ssh-connection')
                   (EncodeString'publickey')
                   (EncodeBoolean 1)
                   (EncodeString'rsa-sha2-256')
                   (EncodeStringBytes pubKeyBlob))

      ⍝ Step 4: Sign with RSA PKCS#1 v1.5 SHA-256
      sigBytes←RsaSha256Sign key.n key.e key.d dataToSign

      ⍝ Step 5: Build signature blob: "rsa-sha2-256" || raw-signature
      sigBlob←∊(EncodeString'rsa-sha2-256')(EncodeStringBytes sigBytes)

      ⍝ Step 6: Send full auth request with signature
      authPayload←∊((,MSG_USERAUTH_REQUEST)
                    (EncodeString Username)
                    (EncodeString'ssh-connection')
                    (EncodeString'publickey')
                    (EncodeBoolean 1)
                    (EncodeString'rsa-sha2-256')
                    (EncodeStringBytes pubKeyBlob)
                    (EncodeStringBytes sigBlob))
      :If 0≠SendPacket authPayload
          r.msg←'Failed to send signed publickey auth' ⋄ →0
      :EndIf

      ⍝ Step 7: Wait for result
      (payload buf)←RecvPacket buf
      :While MSG_USERAUTH_BANNER=⊃payload  ⍝ skip server banners (53)
          (payload buf)←RecvPacket buf
      :EndWhile
      :If MSG_USERAUTH_SUCCESS=⊃payload
          Authenticated←1
          r.msg←''
      :ElseIf MSG_USERAUTH_FAILURE=⊃payload
          r.msg←'Public key authentication failed'
      :ElseIf MSG_DISCONNECT=⊃payload
          r.msg←'Server disconnected during publickey auth'
      :Else
          r.msg←'Unexpected message type ',⍕⊃payload
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ∇ r←SSHOpenChannel r;payload;buf;recipientChannel;rest;maxPktSize;dummy
    ⍝ RFC 4254 §5  Open a new session channel
    ⍝ Must be called after successful authentication
      ChannelID←ChannelID+1
      ⍝ Send SSH_MSG_CHANNEL_OPEN: 'session', local channel, window size, max packet size
      payload←∊((,MSG_CHANNEL_OPEN)
               (EncodeString'session')
               (EncodeUint32 ChannelID)
               (EncodeUint32 2097152)
               (EncodeUint32 32768))
      :If 0≠SendPacket payload
          r.msg←'Failed to send CHANNEL_OPEN' ⋄ →0
      :EndIf
      ⍝ Wait for confirmation or failure (skip transport messages and global requests)
      buf←⍬
      :Repeat
          (payload buf)←RecvPacket buf
          :If MSG_GLOBAL_REQUEST=⊃payload
              ⍝ Decline any server global requests (e.g. hostkeys-00@openssh.com)
              rest←1↓payload
              (dummy rest)←DecodeString rest  ⍝ request name
              :If 0≠⊃rest                     ⍝ want-reply flag
                  {}SendPacket,MSG_REQUEST_FAILURE
              :EndIf
          :EndIf
      :Until ~(⊃payload)∊MSG_IGNORE MSG_DEBUG MSG_GLOBAL_REQUEST
      :If MSG_CHANNEL_OPEN_CONFIRMATION=⊃payload
          rest←1↓payload
          (recipientChannel rest)←DecodeUint32 rest
          (RemoteChannelID rest)←DecodeUint32 rest
          (RemoteWindowSize rest)←DecodeUint32 rest
          (maxPktSize rest)←DecodeUint32 rest
          r.msg←''
      :ElseIf MSG_CHANNEL_OPEN_FAILURE=⊃payload
          r.msg←'Channel open rejected by server'
      :Else
          r.msg←'Expected CHANNEL_OPEN_CONFIRMATION(91), got type ',⍕⊃payload
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ∇ r←cmd SSHExec r;payload;buf;msgType;rest;chData;done;dummy;received
    ⍝ RFC 4254 §6.5  Open a session channel and request remote command execution
    ⍝ Collects stdout; returns data in r.Data

      ⍝ Step 1: Open a session channel
      →0↓⍨0∊⍴(SSHOpenChannel r).msg

      ⍝ Step 2: Send SSH_MSG_CHANNEL_REQUEST for exec
      payload←∊((,MSG_CHANNEL_REQUEST)
               (EncodeUint32 RemoteChannelID)
               (EncodeString'exec')
               (EncodeBoolean 1)
               (EncodeString cmd))
      :If 0≠SendPacket payload
          r.msg←'Failed to send exec request' ⋄ →0
      :EndIf

      ⍝ Step 3: Wait for CHANNEL_SUCCESS (skip window adjusts)
      buf←⍬
      :Repeat
          (payload buf)←RecvPacket buf
          msgType←⊃payload
      :Until msgType≠MSG_CHANNEL_WINDOW_ADJUST
      :If MSG_CHANNEL_FAILURE=msgType
          r.msg←'Exec request rejected' ⋄ →0
      :ElseIf MSG_CHANNEL_SUCCESS≠msgType
          r.msg←'Expected CHANNEL_SUCCESS(99), got type ',⍕msgType ⋄ →0
      :EndIf

      ⍝ Step 4: Collect data until CHANNEL_CLOSE
      r.Data←⍬
      received←0
      done←0
      :While ~done
          (payload buf)←RecvPacket buf
          msgType←⊃payload
          :Select msgType
          :Case MSG_CHANNEL_DATA
              rest←1↓payload
              (dummy rest)←DecodeUint32 rest   ⍝ recipient channel
              (chData rest)←DecodeStringRaw rest  ⍝ data payload (raw bytes)
              r.Data,←chData
              received+←≢chData
              ⍝ Replenish receive window when half consumed
              :If received≥1048576
                  {}SendPacket(,MSG_CHANNEL_WINDOW_ADJUST),(EncodeUint32 RemoteChannelID),(EncodeUint32 received)
                  received←0
              :EndIf
          :Case MSG_CHANNEL_EOF
              ⍝ No more data from server
          :Case MSG_CHANNEL_CLOSE
              done←1
          :Case MSG_CHANNEL_WINDOW_ADJUST
              ⍝ Server increased our send window; ignored for exec
          :Case MSG_CHANNEL_REQUEST
              ⍝ Server may send exit-status or exit-signal; skip
          :Else
              r.msg←'Unexpected message type ',⍕msgType
              done←1
          :EndSelect
      :EndWhile

      ⍝ Step 5: Send our CHANNEL_CLOSE in response
      {}SendPacket(,MSG_CHANNEL_CLOSE),(EncodeUint32 RemoteChannelID)

      r.Data←'UTF-8'⎕UCS r.Data
      r.(rc msg)←0 ''
    ∇

    ∇ payload←SSHDisconnectPacket args;reason;desc
    ⍝ Build an SSH_MSG_DISCONNECT payload (msg type 1)
    ⍝ args - (reason-code description)
    ⍝ Returns payload suitable for SendPacket
    ⍝ RFC 4253 §11.1: [byte MSG_DISCONNECT][uint32 reason][string description][string language-tag]
      (reason desc)←2↑args
      payload←(,MSG_DISCONNECT),(EncodeUint32 reason),(EncodeString desc),EncodeString''
    ∇

⍝ ────────────────────────────────────────────────
⍝  SFTP subsystem methods (SSH File Transfer Protocol v3)
⍝ ────────────────────────────────────────────────

    ∇ r←SFTPOpenSession r;payload;buf;msgType;rest;recipientChannel;maxPktSize;dummy;sftpMsg
    ⍝ Open an SSH channel with the SFTP subsystem and initialise the protocol
      SFTPBuf←⍬ ⋄ SFTPRecvBuf←⍬ ⋄ SFTPReqID←0 ⋄ SFTPReceived←0

      ⍝ Open a new session channel
      ChannelID+←1
      SFTPChanID←ChannelID
      payload←∊((,MSG_CHANNEL_OPEN)
               (EncodeString'session')
               (EncodeUint32 SFTPChanID)
               (EncodeUint32 2097152)
               (EncodeUint32 32768))
      :If 0≠SendPacket payload
          r.msg←'Failed to send CHANNEL_OPEN for SFTP' ⋄ →0
      :EndIf

      ⍝ Wait for CHANNEL_OPEN_CONFIRMATION
      buf←⍬
      :Repeat
          (payload buf)←RecvPacket buf
          :If MSG_GLOBAL_REQUEST=⊃payload
              rest←1↓payload
              (dummy rest)←DecodeString rest
              :If 0≠⊃rest ⋄ {}SendPacket,MSG_REQUEST_FAILURE ⋄ :EndIf
          :EndIf
      :Until ~(⊃payload)∊MSG_IGNORE MSG_DEBUG MSG_GLOBAL_REQUEST
      :If MSG_CHANNEL_OPEN_CONFIRMATION≠⊃payload
          :If MSG_CHANNEL_OPEN_FAILURE=⊃payload
              r.msg←'SFTP channel open rejected by server'
          :Else
              r.msg←'Expected CHANNEL_OPEN_CONFIRMATION, got type ',⍕⊃payload
          :EndIf
          →0
      :EndIf
      rest←1↓payload
      (recipientChannel rest)←DecodeUint32 rest
      (SFTPRemoteChan rest)←DecodeUint32 rest
      (SFTPRemoteWin rest)←DecodeUint32 rest
      (maxPktSize rest)←DecodeUint32 rest

      ⍝ Request "sftp" subsystem
      payload←∊((,MSG_CHANNEL_REQUEST)
               (EncodeUint32 SFTPRemoteChan)
               (EncodeString'subsystem')
               (EncodeBoolean 1)
               (EncodeString'sftp'))
      :If 0≠SendPacket payload
          r.msg←'Failed to send subsystem request' ⋄ →0
      :EndIf

      ⍝ Wait for CHANNEL_SUCCESS
      :Repeat
          (payload buf)←RecvPacket buf
          msgType←⊃payload
      :Until msgType≠MSG_CHANNEL_WINDOW_ADJUST
      :If MSG_CHANNEL_FAILURE=msgType
          r.msg←'SFTP subsystem request rejected' ⋄ →0
      :ElseIf MSG_CHANNEL_SUCCESS≠msgType
          r.msg←'Expected CHANNEL_SUCCESS, got type ',⍕msgType ⋄ →0
      :EndIf

      SFTPRecvBuf←buf

      ⍝ Send SSH_FXP_INIT (version 3)
      {}SFTPSend(,FXP_INIT),(EncodeUint32 3)

      ⍝ Receive SSH_FXP_VERSION
      sftpMsg←SFTPRecv
      :If 0∊⍴sftpMsg
          r.msg←'Did not receive SFTP VERSION response' ⋄ →0
      :EndIf
      :If FXP_VERSION≠⊃sftpMsg
          r.msg←'Expected FXP_VERSION(2), got type ',⍕⊃sftpMsg ⋄ →0
      :EndIf

      SFTPActive←1
      r.msg←''
    ∇

    ∇ SFTPCloseSession;payload;msgType
    ⍝ Close the SFTP subsystem channel
      :If SFTPActive
          :Trap 0
              {}SendPacket(,MSG_CHANNEL_EOF),(EncodeUint32 SFTPRemoteChan)
              {}SendPacket(,MSG_CHANNEL_CLOSE),(EncodeUint32 SFTPRemoteChan)
              :Repeat
                  (payload SFTPRecvBuf)←RecvPacket SFTPRecvBuf
                  msgType←⊃payload
              :Until msgType∊MSG_CHANNEL_CLOSE MSG_DISCONNECT
          :EndTrap
          SFTPActive←0
          SFTPBuf←⍬ ⋄ SFTPRecvBuf←⍬
          SFTPChanID←¯1 ⋄ SFTPRemoteChan←¯1
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ∇ rc←SFTPSend body;sftpPkt;payload
    ⍝ Send an SFTP packet over the subsystem channel
    ⍝ body - byte vector: [type][payload]
      :If dbg 4
          ⎕←'DBG SFTPSend: body DR=',(⍕⎕DR body),' shape=',(⍕⍴body),' depth=',⍕≡body
          ⎕←'DBG SFTPSend: body range: min=',(⍕⌊/body),' max=',(⍕⌈/body)
      :EndIf
      sftpPkt←(EncodeUint32≢body),body
      :If dbg 4
          ⎕←'DBG SFTPSend: sftpPkt DR=',(⍕⎕DR sftpPkt),' shape=',(⍕⍴sftpPkt),' depth=',⍕≡sftpPkt
          ⎕←'DBG SFTPSend: sftpPkt range: min=',(⍕⌊/sftpPkt),' max=',(⍕⌈/sftpPkt)
      :EndIf
      payload←∊((,MSG_CHANNEL_DATA)
               (EncodeUint32 SFTPRemoteChan)
               (EncodeStringBytes sftpPkt))
      :If dbg 4
          ⎕←'DBG SFTPSend: payload DR=',(⍕⎕DR payload),' shape=',(⍕⍴payload),' depth=',⍕≡payload
          ⎕←'DBG SFTPSend: payload range: min=',(⍕⌊/payload),' max=',(⍕⌈/payload)
      :EndIf
      rc←SendPacket payload
    ∇

    ∇ msg←SFTPRecv;payload;msgType;rest;sftpLen;len;dummy;adj
    ⍝ Receive one complete SFTP message from the subsystem channel
    ⍝ Returns byte vector [type][payload] (without length prefix), or ⍬ on EOF/close
      :While 1
          :If 4≤≢SFTPBuf
              sftpLen←256⊥4↑SFTPBuf
              :If (4+sftpLen)≤≢SFTPBuf
                  msg←sftpLen↑4↓SFTPBuf
                  SFTPBuf←(4+sftpLen)↓SFTPBuf
                  →0
              :EndIf
          :EndIf
          (payload SFTPRecvBuf)←RecvPacket SFTPRecvBuf
          msgType←⊃payload
          :Select msgType
          :Case MSG_CHANNEL_DATA
              rest←1↓payload
              (dummy rest)←DecodeUint32 rest
              (len rest)←DecodeUint32 rest
              SFTPBuf,←len↑rest
              SFTPReceived+←len
              :If SFTPReceived≥1048576
                  {}SendPacket(,MSG_CHANNEL_WINDOW_ADJUST),(EncodeUint32 SFTPRemoteChan),(EncodeUint32 SFTPReceived)
                  SFTPReceived←0
              :EndIf
          :Case MSG_CHANNEL_WINDOW_ADJUST
              rest←1↓payload
              (dummy rest)←DecodeUint32 rest
              (adj rest)←DecodeUint32 rest
              SFTPRemoteWin+←adj
          :Case MSG_CHANNEL_EOF
              msg←⍬ ⋄ →0
          :Case MSG_CHANNEL_CLOSE
              SFTPActive←0 ⋄ msg←⍬ ⋄ →0
          :Case MSG_GLOBAL_REQUEST
              rest←1↓payload
              (dummy rest)←DecodeString rest
              :If 0≠⊃rest
                  {}SendPacket,MSG_REQUEST_FAILURE
              :EndIf
          :EndSelect
      :EndWhile
    ∇

    ∇ id←NextSFTPID
    ⍝ Return the next SFTP request ID and increment the counter
      id←SFTPReqID
      SFTPReqID+←1
    ∇

    ∇ (attrs rest)←DecodeAttrs bytes;flags;sz;uid;gid;perms;atime;mtime;extCount;i;dummy
    ⍝ Decode SFTP v3 file attributes from byte stream
    ⍝ Returns namespace with flags size uid gid permissions atime mtime
      attrs←⎕NS''
      attrs.(flags size uid gid permissions atime mtime)←0 0 0 0 0 0 0
      (flags rest)←DecodeUint32 bytes
      attrs.flags←flags
      :If 0≠2|flags                    ⍝ SSH_FILEXFER_ATTR_SIZE (bit 0)
          (sz rest)←DecodeUint64 rest
          attrs.size←sz
      :EndIf
      :If 0≠2|⌊flags÷2                ⍝ SSH_FILEXFER_ATTR_UIDGID (bit 1)
          (uid rest)←DecodeUint32 rest
          (gid rest)←DecodeUint32 rest
          attrs.(uid gid)←uid gid
      :EndIf
      :If 0≠2|⌊flags÷4                ⍝ SSH_FILEXFER_ATTR_PERMISSIONS (bit 2)
          (perms rest)←DecodeUint32 rest
          attrs.permissions←perms
      :EndIf
      :If 0≠2|⌊flags÷8                ⍝ SSH_FILEXFER_ATTR_ACMODTIME (bit 3)
          (atime rest)←DecodeUint32 rest
          (mtime rest)←DecodeUint32 rest
          attrs.(atime mtime)←atime mtime
      :EndIf
      :If 0≠2|⌊flags÷2147483648       ⍝ SSH_FILEXFER_ATTR_EXTENDED (bit 31)
          (extCount rest)←DecodeUint32 rest
          :For i :In ⍳extCount
              (dummy rest)←DecodeString rest
              (dummy rest)←DecodeString rest
          :EndFor
      :EndIf
    ∇

⍝ ────────────────────────────────────────────────
⍝  SSH binary packet encoding helpers (RFC 4251)
⍝ ────────────────────────────────────────────────

    ∇ bytes←EncodeUint32 n
    ⍝ Encode an integer as a 4-byte big-endian byte vector
      :If n>4294967295
          'Value exceeds uint32 range'⎕SIGNAL 11
      :EndIf
      bytes←∊(4⍴256)⊤n
    ∇

    ∇ bytes←EncodeString s
    ⍝ RFC 4251 §5  Encode a string as [uint32 length][bytes]
      bytes←(EncodeUint32⍴s),⎕UCS s
    ∇

    ∇ bytes←EncodeStringBytes b
    ⍝ RFC 4251 §5  Encode a raw byte vector as [uint32 length][bytes]
    ⍝ Like EncodeString but input is already integer bytes, not characters
      bytes←(EncodeUint32≢b),b
    ∇

    ∇ bytes←EncodeBoolean b
    ⍝ RFC 4251 §5  Encode a boolean (0=FALSE, anything else=TRUE)
      bytes←,⍬⍴0≠b
    ∇

    ∇ bytes←EncodeUint64 n
    ⍝ Encode an integer as an 8-byte big-endian byte vector
      bytes←∊(8⍴256)⊤n
    ∇

    ∇ (n rest)←DecodeUint32 bytes
    ⍝ Decode the first 4 bytes of bytes as a big-endian uint32; return value and remainder
      n←256⊥4↑bytes
      rest←4↓bytes
    ∇

    ∇ (n rest)←DecodeUint64 bytes
    ⍝ Decode the first 8 bytes as a big-endian uint64; return value and remainder
      n←256⊥8↑bytes
      rest←8↓bytes
    ∇

    ∇ (s rest)←DecodeString bytes
    ⍝ Decode a length-prefixed SSH string; return the string and remaining bytes
      (len rest)←DecodeUint32 bytes
      s←⎕UCS len↑rest
      rest←len↓rest
    ∇

    ∇ (b rest)←DecodeStringRaw bytes;len
    ⍝ Decode a length-prefixed string as raw integer bytes (no ⎕UCS conversion)
      (len rest)←DecodeUint32 bytes
      b←len↑rest
      rest←len↓rest
    ∇

    ∇ packet←WrapPacket payload
    ⍝ RFC 4253 §6  Wrap a payload in the SSH binary packet format
    ⍝ Returns byte vector: [uint32 pkt_len][byte pad_len][payload][padding]
      blockSize←8+8×CryptoActive           ⍝ 8 before crypto, 16 after (AES block size)
      padLen←blockSize-blockSize|5+≢payload  ⍝ must be ≥4
      padLen+←blockSize×padLen<4
      pktLen←1+(≢payload)+padLen           ⍝ pad_length byte + payload + padding
      packet←(EncodeUint32 pktLen),(,padLen),payload,(⎕IO-⍨?padLen⍴256)
    ∇

    ∇ (payload rest)←UnwrapPacket bytes
    ⍝ RFC 4253 §6  Extract the payload from a received binary SSH packet
      (pktLen rest)←DecodeUint32 bytes
      padLen←⊃rest
      payload←(¯1+pktLen-padLen)↑1↓rest   ⍝ drop pad_len byte and padding
      rest←(pktLen+4)↓bytes               ⍝ remaining bytes after this packet
      ⍝ NOTE: HMAC verification and decryption are handled by RecvPacket before calling this
    ∇

⍝ ────────────────────────────────────────────────
⍝  DH / mpint helpers
⍝ ────────────────────────────────────────────────
    ∇ r←PowMod args;base;exp;mod;dll;zb;ze;zm;zr;nB;z0
        base exp mod←args
        dll←nettleDll

        z0←⊂0 0 0  ⍝ zeroed mpz_t struct {I4 I4 P}, enclosed = one arg

        'zinit'⎕NA dll,'|__gmpz_init   ={I4 I4 P}'
        'zclear'⎕NA dll,'|__gmpz_clear  ={I4 I4 P}'
        'zpowm'⎕NA dll,'|__gmpz_powm   ={I4 I4 P} <{I4 I4 P} <{I4 I4 P} <{I4 I4 P}'
        'zset'⎕NA dll,'|nettle_mpz_set_str_256_u ={I4 I4 P} U4 <U1[]'
        'zget'⎕NA dll,'|nettle_mpz_get_str_256   U4 >U1[] <{I4 I4 P}'

        ⍝ Init — void + one = param → 1-element result vector
        zb←zinit z0 ⋄ ze←zinit z0
        zm←zinit z0 ⋄ zr←zinit z0

        ⍝ Load from big-endian bytes — result is the modified struct
        zb←zset(⊂zb)(≢base)base
        ze←zset(⊂ze)(≢exp)exp
        zm←zset(⊂zm)(≢mod)mod

        ⍝ zr ← zb*ze mod zm — only zr comes back (the = param)
        zr←zpowm(⊂zr)(⊂zb)(⊂ze)(⊂zm)

        ⍝ Extract result bytes — void + one > param → 1-element result
        nB←≢mod
        r←zget nB nB(⊂zr)

        ⍝ Free GMP limb allocations
        _←zclear⊂zb ⋄ _←zclear⊂ze
        _←zclear⊂zm ⋄ _←zclear⊂zr
        ∇

    ∇ bytes←EncodeMpInt n
    ⍝ RFC 4251 §5  Encode a big-endian byte vector as an SSH mpint
    ⍝ Result: [uint32 length][big-endian bytes, 0x00-padded if MSB set]
      bytes←(∨\n≠0)⌿n          ⍝ strip leading zeros from byte vector
      :If 0∊⍴bytes ⋄ bytes←,0 ⋄ :EndIf
      :If 128≤⊃bytes ⋄ bytes←0,bytes ⋄ :EndIf  ⍝ prevent sign-bit misread
      bytes←(EncodeUint32⍴bytes),bytes
    ∇

    ∇ (n rest)←DecodeMpInt bytes
    ⍝ RFC 4251 §5  Decode an SSH mpint; return value and remaining bytes
      (raw rest)←DecodeString bytes  ⍝ reads length-prefixed byte string
      n←256⊥⎕UCS raw               ⍝ big-endian bytes → APL integer
    ∇

    ∇ (b rest)←DecodeMpIntBytes bytes;raw
    ⍝ RFC 4251 §5  Decode an SSH mpint as a byte vector (no precision loss)
      (raw rest)←DecodeString bytes
      b←⎕UCS raw
    ∇

    ∇ rc←SendPacket payload;packet;mac;encrypted
    ⍝ Build, optionally encrypt+MAC, and send an SSH packet; increment sequence number
      :If dbg 4
          ⎕←'DBG SendPacket: payload DR=',(⍕⎕DR payload),' shape=',(⍕⍴payload),' depth=',⍕≡payload
          :If 0<≢payload ⋄ ⎕←'DBG SendPacket: payload range: min=',(⍕⌊/payload),' max=',(⍕⌈/payload) ⋄ :EndIf
      :EndIf
      packet←WrapPacket payload
      :If dbg 4
          ⎕←'DBG SendPacket: packet DR=',(⍕⎕DR packet),' shape=',(⍕⍴packet),' depth=',⍕≡packet
          :If 0<≢packet ⋄ ⎕←'DBG SendPacket: packet range: min=',(⍕⌊/packet),' max=',(⍕⌈/packet) ⋄ :EndIf
      :EndIf
      :If CryptoActive
          mac←MacKeySend hmacSha256(EncodeUint32 SeqSend),packet
          (encrypted CtrSend)←aes128CtrCrypt AesCtxSend CtrSend packet
          rc←⊃LDRC.Send Client(encrypted,mac)
      :Else
          rc←⊃LDRC.Send Client packet
      :EndIf
      SeqSend+←1
    ∇

    ∇ (payload rest)←RecvPacket buf;rc;obj;evt;data;pktLen;needed;firstBlock;restDecr;decrypted;mac;expectedMac
    ⍝ Accumulate raw Conga bytes into buf until one complete SSH binary packet
    ⍝ is available, then unwrap and return (payload, leftover bytes)
      :If CryptoActive
          ⍝ ── Encrypted receive ──────────────────────────────────────────
          ⍝ Read at least one AES block (16 bytes) to learn packet length
          :While (≢buf)<16
              (rc obj evt data)←4↑LDRC.Wait Client WaitTime
              :If (0≠rc)∨evt≢'Block'
                  ⎕SIGNAL⊂('EN' 11)('Message'('RecvPacket: read error, rc=',⍕rc))
              :EndIf
              buf,←data
          :EndWhile
          ⍝ Decrypt first block to get packet_length
          (firstBlock CtrRecv)←aes128CtrCrypt AesCtxRecv CtrRecv(16↑buf)
          pktLen←256⊥4↑firstBlock
          ⍝ Total: 4+pktLen encrypted bytes, then 32-byte MAC
          needed←4+pktLen+32
          :While (≢buf)<needed
              (rc obj evt data)←4↑LDRC.Wait Client WaitTime
              :If (0≠rc)∨evt≢'Block'
                  ⎕SIGNAL⊂('EN' 11)('Message'('RecvPacket: read error, rc=',⍕rc))
              :EndIf
              buf,←data
          :EndWhile
          ⍝ Decrypt remaining encrypted bytes (after the first 16 already decrypted)
          :If dbg 4
              ⎕←'DBG RecvPacket: pktLen=',⍕pktLen
              ⎕←'DBG RecvPacket: firstBlock DR=',(⍕⎕DR firstBlock),' shape=',⍕⍴firstBlock
              ⎕←'DBG RecvPacket: firstBlock values=',⍕firstBlock
              ⎕←'DBG RecvPacket: rest to decrypt=',(⍕pktLen-12),' bytes'
          :EndIf
          (restDecr CtrRecv)←aes128CtrCrypt AesCtxRecv CtrRecv((pktLen-12)↑16↓buf)
          decrypted←firstBlock,restDecr
          :If dbg 4
              ⎕←'DBG RecvPacket: restDecr DR=',(⍕⎕DR restDecr),' shape=',⍕⍴restDecr
              ⎕←'DBG RecvPacket: decrypted DR=',(⍕⎕DR decrypted),' shape=',(⍕⍴decrypted),' first16=',⍕16↑decrypted
          :EndIf
          ⍝ Verify MAC
          mac←32↑(4+pktLen)↓buf
          :If dbg 4 ⋄ ⎕←'DBG RecvPacket: seqRecv=',⍕SeqRecv ⋄ :EndIf
          expectedMac←MacKeyRecv hmacSha256(EncodeUint32 SeqRecv),decrypted
          :If mac≢expectedMac
              ⎕SIGNAL⊂('EN' 11)('Message' 'MAC verification failed')
          :EndIf
          (payload rest)←UnwrapPacket decrypted
          rest←(4+pktLen+32)↓buf
      :Else
          ⍝ ── Plaintext receive ──────────────────────────────────────────
          :While (≢buf)<4
              (rc obj evt data)←4↑LDRC.Wait Client WaitTime
              :If (0≠rc)∨evt≢'Block'
                  ⎕SIGNAL⊂('EN' 11)('Message'('RecvPacket: read error, rc=',⍕rc,', evt=',⍕evt))
              :EndIf
              buf,←data
          :EndWhile
          pktLen←256⊥4↑buf
          needed←4+pktLen
          :While (≢buf)<needed
              (rc obj evt data)←4↑LDRC.Wait Client WaitTime
              :If (0≠rc)∨evt≢'Block'
                  ⎕SIGNAL⊂('EN' 11)('Message'('RecvPacket: read error, rc=',⍕rc,', evt=',⍕evt))
              :EndIf
              buf,←data
          :EndWhile
          (payload rest)←UnwrapPacket buf
      :EndIf
      SeqRecv+←1
    ∇

⍝ ────────────────────────────────────────────────
⍝  Utility
⍝ ────────────────────────────────────────────────

    ∇ nameClass←nameClass ref
    ⍝ Return the ⎕NC of ref (accepts both name strings and references)
      nameClass←{0::⎕NC⍕⍵ ⋄ ⎕NC⊂,'⍵'}ref
    ∇

    ∇ stopIf condition
    ⍝ Programmatic breakpoint helper (mirrors HttpCommand usage)
      :If condition ⋄ .⎕SIGNAL 1000 ⋄ :EndIf
    ∇

    ∇ r←GetEnv var
    ⍝ return enviroment variable setting for var
      :Access public shared
      r←2 ⎕NQ'.' 'GetEnvironment'var
    ∇

    dbg←{0≠2|⌊Debug÷⍵}                            ⍝ test whether debug bit ⍵ is set

    ∇ r←dyalogRoot
    ⍝ return path to interpreter
      r←{⍵,('/\'∊⍨⊢/⍵)↓'/'}{0∊⍴t←GetEnv'DYALOG':⊃1 ⎕NPARTS⊃2 ⎕NQ'.' 'GetCommandLineArgs' ⋄ t}''
    ∇

    ToBEBytes←{⍵=0:,0 ⋄ (0~⍨⊢)256⊥⍣¯1⊢⍵}

⍝ ────────────────────────────────────────────────
⍝  Base64 decoding
⍝ ────────────────────────────────────────────────

    ∇ bytes←Base64Decode b64;⎕IO;⎕ML;chars;bits;part
    ⍝ Decode a Base64-encoded character vector to an integer byte vector
    ⍝ Based on dfns base64
      ⎕IO ⎕ML←0 1
      chars←'ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789+/'
      bits←{,⍉(⍺⍴2)⊤⍵}
      part←{((⍴⍵)⍴⍺↑1)⊂⍵}
      bytes←2∘⊥∘(8∘↑)¨8 part{(-8|⍴⍵)↓⍵}6 bits{(⍵≠64)/⍵}chars⍳b64
    ∇

⍝ ────────────────────────────────────────────────
⍝  OpenSSH private key parser
⍝ ────────────────────────────────────────────────

    ∇ key←ParseOpenSSHKey keyfile;lines;body;raw;pos;magic;cipherName;kdfName;kdfOpts;nKeys;pubBlob;privSection;check1;check2;keyType;rest;n;e;d;iqmp;p;q;comment
    ⍝ Parse an OpenSSH-format private key file (openssh-key-v1)
    ⍝ Returns namespace with n e d p q as byte vectors
    ⍝ Only supports unencrypted keys (cipher = "none")
      lines←⊃⎕NGET keyfile 1
      ⍝ Strip BEGIN/END markers and blank lines
      lines←(~∨/¨'-----'∘⍷¨lines)/lines
      lines←(0<≢¨lines)/lines
      body←∊lines
      raw←Base64Decode body

      ⍝ Verify magic: "openssh-key-v1\0" (15 bytes)
      magic←'openssh-key-v1',(⎕UCS 0)
      :If (⎕UCS(≢magic)↑raw)≢magic
          'Not an OpenSSH private key file'⎕SIGNAL 11
      :EndIf
      rest←(≢magic)↓raw

      ⍝ Read cipher name (expect "none")
      (cipherName rest)←DecodeString rest
      :If cipherName≢'none'
          'Encrypted private keys are not supported'⎕SIGNAL 11
      :EndIf

      ⍝ Skip KDF name and KDF options
      (kdfName rest)←DecodeString rest
      (kdfOpts rest)←DecodeString rest

      ⍝ Number of keys
      (nKeys rest)←DecodeUint32 rest
      :If nKeys≠1
          'Expected exactly 1 key in file'⎕SIGNAL 11
      :EndIf

      ⍝ Skip public key blob (length-prefixed)
      (pubBlob rest)←DecodeString rest

      ⍝ Read private section (length-prefixed)
      (privSection rest)←DecodeString rest
      rest←⎕UCS privSection

      ⍝ Verify check integers match
      (check1 rest)←DecodeUint32 rest
      (check2 rest)←DecodeUint32 rest
      :If check1≠check2
          'Private key check values do not match (wrong passphrase?)'⎕SIGNAL 11
      :EndIf

      ⍝ Read key type
      (keyType rest)←DecodeString rest
      :If keyType≢'ssh-rsa'
          ('Unsupported key type: ',keyType)⎕SIGNAL 11
      :EndIf

      ⍝ Read RSA components as mpint byte vectors
      ⍝ OpenSSH order: n, e, d, iqmp, p, q
      (n rest)←DecodeMpIntBytes rest
      (e rest)←DecodeMpIntBytes rest
      (d rest)←DecodeMpIntBytes rest
      (iqmp rest)←DecodeMpIntBytes rest
      (p rest)←DecodeMpIntBytes rest
      (q rest)←DecodeMpIntBytes rest

      ⍝ Skip comment
      ⍝ (comment rest)←DecodeString rest

      key←⎕NS''
      key.(n e d p q)←n e d p q
    ∇

⍝ ────────────────────────────────────────────────
⍝  RSA PKCS#1 v1.5 signing
⍝ ────────────────────────────────────────────────

    ∇ ok←RsaSha256Verify(n e sig data);hash;recovered;keyLen;prefix;sep;di
    ⍝ Verify an RSA PKCS#1 v1.5 SHA-256 signature
    ⍝ n e   - RSA public key components (byte vectors)
    ⍝ sig   - signature bytes
    ⍝ data  - data that was signed (byte vector)
    ⍝ Returns 1 if signature is valid, 0 if not
      ok←0
      hash←sha256 data
      keyLen←≢(∨\n≠0)/n
      recovered←(-keyLen)↑PowMod(sig e n)
      ⍝ PKCS#1 v1.5: 0x00 0x01 [0xFF×≥8] 0x00 [DigestInfo]
      →0⍴⍨(0 1)≢recovered[1 2]
      sep←2+⊃⍸0=2↓recovered
      →0⍴⍨sep<11
      →0⍴⍨~∧/255=recovered[2+⍳sep-3]
      di←sep↓recovered
      prefix←48 49 48 13 6 9 96 134 72 1 101 3 4 2 1 5 0 4 32
      ok←di≡prefix,hash
    ∇

    ∇ sig←RsaSha256Sign(n e d data);hash;digestInfo;prefix;padLen;padded;keyLen
    ⍝ PKCS#1 v1.5 RSA signature with SHA-256
    ⍝ n e d  - RSA key components (byte vectors)
    ⍝ data   - data to sign (byte vector)
    ⍝ sig    - signature (byte vector, same length as n)

      ⍝ Hash the data
      hash←sha256 data

      ⍝ ASN.1 DigestInfo prefix for SHA-256 (19 bytes)
      prefix←48 49 48 13 6 9 96 134 72 1 101 3 4 2 1 5 0 4 32
      digestInfo←prefix,hash   ⍝ 51 bytes total

      ⍝ Key length in bytes (strip any leading zero from n for signing)
      keyLen←≢(∨\n≠0)⌿n

      ⍝ PKCS#1 v1.5 padding: 0x00 0x01 [0xFF×padLen] 0x00 [digestInfo]
      padLen←keyLen-3+≢digestInfo
      :If padLen<8
          'RSA key too short for SHA-256 signature'⎕SIGNAL 11
      :EndIf
      padded←0 1,(padLen⍴255),0,digestInfo

      ⍝ RSA signing: signature = padded^d mod n
      sig←PowMod(padded d n)

      ⍝ Ensure output is exactly keyLen bytes (left-pad with zeros if needed)
      sig←((-keyLen)↑sig)
    ∇

    ∇ r←nettleDll
    ⍝ Return path to the Conga SSL shared library (contains nettle symbols)
      r←∊1↓⊃1 ⎕NPARTS⊃(⎕NINFO⍠('Wildcard' 1)('Recurse' 1))'/*conga??ssl*.*',⍨(⊢2 ⎕NQ #'GetEnvironment',⊂)'Dyalog'
    ∇

⍝ ────────────────────────────────────────────────
⍝  AES-128-CTR encryption helpers
⍝ ────────────────────────────────────────────────

    BytesXOR←{2⊥((8⍴2)⊤⍺)≠(8⍴2)⊤⍵}

    ∇ ctr←IncrCtr ctr;i;s
    ⍝ Increment a big-endian 16-byte counter by 1
      :For i :In ⌽⍳≢ctr
          s←1+ctr[i]
          ctr[i]←256|s
          :If s<256 ⋄ :Leave ⋄ :EndIf
      :EndFor
    ∇

    ∇ (result newCtr)←aes128CtrCrypt(ctx ctr data);dll;AesEnc;i;ks;offset;n;blk
    ⍝ AES-128-CTR encrypt/decrypt (symmetric operation)
    ⍝ ctx   - 176-byte AES-128 context from InitCrypto
    ⍝ ctr   - 16-byte counter (IV), updated across calls
    ⍝ data  - byte vector to encrypt/decrypt
      dll←nettleDll
      'AesEnc'⎕NA dll,'|nettle_aes128_encrypt <U1[176] U8 >U1[16] <U1[16]'
      result←⍬
      newCtr←ctr
      :For i :In ⍳⌈(≢data)÷16
          ks←AesEnc ctx 16 16 newCtr
          offset←16×i-⎕IO
          n←16⌊(≢data)-offset
          blk←n↑offset↓data
          result,←(n↑ks)BytesXOR blk
          newCtr←IncrCtr newCtr
      :EndFor
    ∇

    ∇ InitCrypto(ekc eks);dll;AesSetKey
    ⍝ Initialize AES-128 encrypt contexts for send and receive
      dll←nettleDll
      'AesSetKey'⎕NA dll,'|nettle_aes128_set_encrypt_key >U1[176] <U1[16]'
      AesCtxSend←AesSetKey 176 ekc
      AesCtxRecv←AesSetKey 176 eks
    ∇

    ∇ digest←sha256 data;Init;Update;Digest;ctx;dll;⎕IO
    ⍝ Compute SHA-256 of data (integer byte vector or character vector) using nettle
      ⎕IO←0 ⋄ dll←nettleDll
      'Init'⎕NA dll,'|nettle_sha256_init >I1[336]'
      'Update'⎕NA dll,'|nettle_sha256_update =I1[336] U8 <U1[]'  ⍝ Add data to hash
      'Digest'⎕NA dll,'|nettle_sha256_digest =I1[336] U8 >U1[32]'  ⍝ Finalize and get digest
      ctx←Init 336
      ctx←Update ctx(⍴∊data)(∊data)
      ctx digest←Digest ctx 32 32
    ∇

    ∇ digest←key hmacSha256 data;SetKey;Update;Digest;ctx;dll;⎕IO
    ⍝ Compute HMAC-SHA-256 using nettle
    ⍝ hmac_sha256_ctx = 2×sha256_ctx(336 bytes) + digest(32 bytes) = 704 bytes
      ⎕IO←0 ⋄ dll←nettleDll
      'SetKey'⎕NA dll,'|nettle_hmac_sha256_set_key >U1[704] U8 <U1[]'
      'Update'⎕NA dll,'|nettle_hmac_sha256_update =U1[704] U8 <U1[]'
      'Digest'⎕NA dll,'|nettle_hmac_sha256_digest =U1[704] U8 >U1[32]'
      :If dbg 8
          ⎕←'DBG HMAC: key shape=',(⍕⍴key),' depth=',(⍕≡key),' DR=',⍕⎕DR key
          ⎕←'DBG HMAC: data shape=',(⍕⍴data),' depth=',(⍕≡data),' DR=',⍕⎕DR data
          ⎕←'DBG HMAC: data range: min=',(⍕⌊/data),' max=',⍕⌈/data
      :EndIf
      ctx←SetKey 704(⍴key)key
      :If dbg 8 ⋄ ⎕←'DBG HMAC: SetKey OK, ctx shape=',⍕⍴ctx ⋄ :EndIf
      ctx←Update ctx(⍴data)data
      :If dbg 8 ⋄ ⎕←'DBG HMAC: Update OK' ⋄ :EndIf
      ctx digest←Digest ctx 32 32
    ∇

:EndClass
